--- root cause of the blindness (pre-existing, NOT introduced by NEARS-1776) ---
UserApp/lib/main.dart:90
    // Route all uncaught framework errors to Crashlytics.
    FlutterError.onError = FirebaseCrashlytics.instance.recordFlutterError;

    // Route uncaught async errors (outside the Flutter framework) to Crashlytics.
    PlatformDispatcher.instance.onError = handleUncaughtAsyncError;
FirebaseCrashlytics collection is gated !kDebugMode (main.dart:81), i.e. OFF in debug,
and assigning FlutterError.onError REPLACES the default FlutterError.presentError console dump.
Net effect: a framework build error is user-visible as a full-screen red ErrorWidget while
emitting no [FAIL], no [ERR], no stack and no Crashlytics record on any debug build.

